  "content": {
    "id": "v2-de45f-p12-practice-slot-6-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Calculate the values of $m$ if the distance between $(m,m+1)$ and $(4,-1)$ is exactly $\\sqrt{50}$ units.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$m=5$ or $-3$. Square the distance equation and factorise the resulting quadratic.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\sqrt{(4-m)^2+(-1-(m+1))^2}&=\\sqrt{50}\\\\(4-m)^2+(m+2)^2&=50\\\\16-8m+m^2+m^2+4m+4&=50\\\\2m^2-4m+20&=50\\\\2m^2-4m-30&=0\\\\m^2-2m-15&=0\\end{align*}$$PSF: Product $=-15$, Sum $=-2$, Factors $=3$ and $-5$.$$\\begin{align*}(m+3)(m-5)&=0\\\\m&=-3\\text{ or }5\\end{align*}$$Check $m=5$: $\\sqrt{(-1)^2+(-7)^2}=\\sqrt{50}$. Check $m=-3$: $\\sqrt{7^2+1^2}=\\sqrt{50}$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": null
  },
